If the intention is to create an intelligent sword that has a quest
associated with it, some ideas:

1.  long swords are overused (as another guy said).  make it a sword
sword or something else instead.

2.  the artifact self curses so it is not cursed until you pick it up.
If you un-curse it then after random number of turns, it curses itself
again.  It doesn't want you getting rid of it.

3.  Instead of not gaining exp when using, have it so that if you don't
do what the sword wants  it level drains you.  Going to the
Mines/Sokoban instead of where you're supposed to go - lose a level!
Try wielding a different weapon - get blasted.  The sword punishes you
if you don't do what it wants.

4.  Applying it allows you to converse with it.  This interaction would
tell the player what the sword wants, what the quest is all about and
what the penalties is if he doesn't do what the sword wants.

5.  The sword will intervene (perhaps throw a random spell) if the
wielder looks to be in danger of dieing.  Since its purpose is to get
free, it wants the wielder to survive long enough to accomplish it.

6.  After you complete the quest, the sword becomes just a regular
short sword with no bonus/penalties or is destroyed in the process of
freeing the trapped being.

7.  Perhaps it aggravates nymphs or causes  nymphs to be generated and
attack you if they are the ones behind trapping the being.



